From f520ecbfd5d027d75eea2eddb5681972bacee72f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 06:23:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: reject assignments to WHNAT counters

WHNAT exposes five atomic counters through read-only module parameters.
Their custom operations provide only a get callback. The 0444 permissions
prevent writes through sysfs, but do not prevent assignments through the
kernel command line or module arguments. With an explicit value,
parse_one() calls the missing set callback and dereferences NULL.

Add a setter that rejects assignments with -EPERM. Keep the counter
readers, arguments and permissions unchanged, along with the writable
whnat_enable parameter.

Fixes: f90277e22ed1 ("net: airoha: add WHNAT, the EN751221 PPE offload for WiFi without WED")
Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-6
Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_whnat.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_whnat.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_whnat.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_whnat.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_whnat.c
@@ -52,7 +52,13 @@ static int counter_get(char *buf, const struct kernel_param *kp)
 	return sysfs_emit(buf, "%u\n", (unsigned int)atomic_read(kp->arg));
 }
 
+static int counter_set(const char *val, const struct kernel_param *kp)
+{
+	return -EPERM;
+}
+
 static const struct kernel_param_ops counter_ops = {
+	.set = counter_set,
 	.get = counter_get,
 };
 

